# Build context allowlist.
#
# Everything is excluded, then the exact paths the Dockerfile COPYs are added
# back. The default direction matters: the whole working directory is sent to
# the Docker daemon on every build — a daemon that caches the context and may
# be remote or rootless — so `.env` (which holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for the
# token benchmark) must never be in it, and neither must lib/, bin/ or docs/.
# A denylist would leak every future file nobody thought to add to it.
#
# Adding a COPY to the Dockerfile means adding its path below. Forgetting to
# fails the build with "no source files were specified" rather than silently
# shipping an incomplete image.
*

!.git
!ext
!licenses-spdx
!scripts
!src
!vendor
!LICENSE
!Makefile.release
!licenses.manifest
!shard.lock
!shard.yml
